<%
/* ======================================================================
   ONE QUESTION BLOCK — used twice, from the same source.

     · once per existing question when the form is re-rendered after a
       validation error, and once for the initial empty question;
     · once inside a <template>, with i = "__I__", which admin.js clones
       and renumbers to add a question in the browser.

   Rendering both from this file is the point: a repeater whose "add"
   markup is a separate hand-written copy drifts from the server-rendered
   one the first time a field changes, and the drift shows up as a field
   that silently posts nothing.

   FIELD NAMING. Flat and indexed — q_0_type, q_0_question, q_0_a0 …
   q_0_a5, q_0_correct, q_0_tf, q_0_model, q_0_image. NOT q[0][question].
   app.js parses bodies with express.urlencoded({ extended: false }),
   which is the querystring module and does no bracket nesting at all,
   and this form is multipart so multer parses it instead — multer has no
   nesting option either. Bracket names would arrive as literal keys
   named "q[0][question]".

   Gaps are fine BETWEEN BLOCKS. Removing a block in the browser leaves
   its index unused and the server skips it, so nothing has to renumber
   the name attributes as blocks come and go — only the visible label
   changes.

   Gaps are NOT fine WITHIN a block's option rows, and this is the one
   place the two contracts differ. The server reads q_<i>_a0 … a5 in
   ascending index order and that order becomes the saved option order,
   so a row sitting last on screen under a low free index (a2, when
   a0/a1/a5 exist) would be saved first. admin.js therefore renumbers the
   option rows contiguously on every add and remove.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   QUESTION TYPES, and the one trap in this file.

   Three fieldsets, one per type, of which exactly one is active. Hiding
   the other two is NOT enough: the choice inputs and the answer radio
   carry `required`, and a `required` control that is display:none makes
   the browser refuse to submit on an element it cannot scroll to or
   focus. Chrome logs "An invalid form control with name='…' is not
   focusable" and THE SAVE BUTTON SILENTLY DOES NOTHING — no message, no
   network request, nothing on screen to explain it.

   So an inactive group is `disabled`, not merely hidden. disabled both
   exempts a control from validation and stops it being submitted, which
   also means the server never receives stale fields from a type the
   admin switched away from.

   That state is rendered HERE, server-side, from the block's own type —
   so the form is correct on arrival and works with JavaScript off.
   admin.js only ever flips a state that was already consistent.

   Because the browser drops disabled fields entirely, the server keys
   off q_<i>_type and not off which fields happen to be present.

   LOCALS
     i    index for the name attributes: a number, or "__I__" in template
     pos  the number shown to the admin (1-based), or "" in the template
     q    echo of a rejected submission, or null:
          { type, question, answers: [], correct, tf, modelAnswer,
            maxScore }

   Plus the shared type locals from util/questionTypes.viewLocals():
     QTYPES, QTYPE_LABELS, QTYPE_HINTS, TF_OPTIONS, MIN_OPTIONS,
     MAX_OPTIONS, typeOf
   and the Explain mark bounds from util/grading.viewLocals():
     DEFAULT_EXPLAIN_POINTS, MIN_POINTS, MAX_POINTS

   EJS CANNOT require(). A template compiles to a function with no module
   scope, so `require` in here is undefined and throws at render time —
   the constants have to arrive as locals. Every one is read behind a
   `typeof` guard because EJS compiles with `with(locals)`, where naming
   a key the caller did not pass throws ReferenceError instead of giving
   undefined. The fallbacks below keep this partial renderable on its own.
   ====================================================================== */

var TYPES = typeof QTYPES !== "undefined" ? QTYPES : ["mcq", "truefalse", "explain"];
var LABELS = typeof QTYPE_LABELS !== "undefined" ? QTYPE_LABELS : {};
var HINTS = typeof QTYPE_HINTS !== "undefined" ? QTYPE_HINTS : {};
var TFOPTS = typeof TF_OPTIONS !== "undefined" ? TF_OPTIONS : ["صح", "خطأ"];
var MINOPT = typeof MIN_OPTIONS !== "undefined" ? MIN_OPTIONS : 2;
var MAXOPT = typeof MAX_OPTIONS !== "undefined" ? MAX_OPTIONS : 6;
var DEFOPT = typeof DEFAULT_OPTIONS !== "undefined" ? DEFAULT_OPTIONS : 4;

/* Explain-only mark bounds, from util/grading.viewLocals(). Same inline
   fallbacks as everything else here, so this partial still renders when a
   caller passes only the question-type locals. */
var DEFPTS = typeof DEFAULT_EXPLAIN_POINTS !== "undefined" ? DEFAULT_EXPLAIN_POINTS : 5;
var MINPTS = typeof MIN_POINTS !== "undefined" ? MIN_POINTS : 1;
var MAXPTS = typeof MAX_POINTS !== "undefined" ? MAX_POINTS : 100;

var qq = q && typeof q === "object" ? q : {};

/* The echo names the field `type`; a stored document names it `qType`.
   Read whichever is present, and land on "mcq" for anything unrecognised
   — exactly how the server will read it back. */
var rawType = qq.type || qq.qType;
var qType = TYPES.indexOf(rawType) !== -1 ? rawType : "mcq";

var qAnswers = Array.isArray(qq.answers) ? qq.answers : [];
var qCorrect = qq.correct === undefined || qq.correct === null ? "" : String(qq.correct);
var qTf = qq.tf === undefined || qq.tf === null ? "" : String(qq.tf);

/* The echo and a stored document use the same name here, so one read covers
   both — the echo carries the raw string the admin typed (so a rejected
   submission comes back with it verbatim, even if it was out of range), and a
   document carries the saved number. Falls back to the default, which is also
   what an Explain question saved before this field existed reads as. */
var qMax = qq.maxScore === undefined || qq.maxScore === null || String(qq.maxScore).trim() === ""
  ? String(DEFPTS)
  : String(qq.maxScore).trim();

/* Always render at least MIN_OPTIONS rows so a fresh block is usable
   without JavaScript, and never more than MAX_OPTIONS. */
/* A fresh block starts at DEFAULT_OPTIONS (the historical 4); a rejected
   one comes back with exactly as many rows as were submitted. Clamped
   both ways so a hand-edited echo cannot render 0 rows or 40. */
var optionCount = Math.min(
  MAXOPT,
  Math.max(MINOPT, qAnswers.length || DEFOPT)
);

/* Attributes for the two inactive groups. `hidden` is the attribute, not
   a class: it needs no stylesheet to work, which matters because this
   markup must behave correctly before admin.css is even considered. */
var groupAttrs = function (name) {
  return qType === name ? "" : " hidden";
};
var groupDisabled = function (name) {
  return qType === name ? "" : " disabled";
};
%>
<fieldset class="qcard" data-qcard>
  <legend class="qcard__legend">
    <span class="qcard__no num" dir="ltr" data-qno><%= pos %></span>
    <span class="qcard__legend-text">السؤال</span>
  </legend>

  <%
  /* type="button" matters: a <button> inside a form defaults to type
     submit, so an unadorned remove button would post the whole form. */
  %>
  <button class="qcard__remove" type="button" data-qremove>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6 19a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h8a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7H6v12zM19 4h-3.5l-1-1h-5l-1 1H5v2h14V4z" />
    </svg>
    <span class="sr-only">حذف السؤال <span data-qno><%= pos %></span></span>
    <span aria-hidden="true">حذف</span>
  </button>

  <%
  /* .select, not .input — the two are sized identically but only .select
     carries the arrow padding and cursor: pointer, so a <select class="input">
     is a dropdown that does not look clickable. --lg is the width cap that
     used to be a `max-inline-size` on the control itself in admin.css. */
  %>
  <div class="form-field form-field--lg qcard__type">
    <label class="label" for="q_<%= i %>_type">نوع السؤال</label>
    <select
      class="select"
      id="q_<%= i %>_type"
      name="q_<%= i %>_type"
      data-qtype
    >
      <% TYPES.forEach(function (t) { %>
      <option value="<%= t %>"<%= qType === t ? " selected" : "" %>>
        <%= LABELS[t] || t %>
      </option>
      <% }); %>
    </select>
    <%
    /* Every hint is rendered and all but one hidden, rather than swapped
       by JS from a data attribute — the select works without JS, so the
       hint has to be correct without JS too. */
    %>
    <% TYPES.forEach(function (t) { %>
    <p class="field-hint" data-qhint="<%= t %>"<%= groupAttrs(t) %>>
      <%= HINTS[t] || "" %>
    </p>
    <% }); %>
  </div>

  <div class="form-field">
    <label class="label" for="q_<%= i %>_question">
      نص السؤال <abbr title="مطلوب">*</abbr>
    </label>
    <%
    /* Outside the per-type groups on purpose: every type has question
       text, so switching type must never clear what was typed here. */
    %>
    <textarea
      class="input qcard__question"
      id="q_<%= i %>_question"
      name="q_<%= i %>_question"
      required
      maxlength="500"
      rows="2"
      autocomplete="off"
    ><%= qq.question || "" %></textarea>
  </div>

  <%
  /* ---- MULTIPLE CHOICE ------------------------------------------- */
  %>
  <fieldset
    class="qfields"
    data-qfields="mcq"<%= groupAttrs("mcq") %><%= groupDisabled("mcq") %>
  >
    <legend class="sr-only">اختيارات الإجابة</legend>

    <div
      class="qchoices"
      role="group"
      aria-label="اختيارات الإجابة"
      data-qchoices
      data-qmin="<%= MINOPT %>"
      data-qmax="<%= MAXOPT %>"
    >
      <p class="qchoices__hint">
        اكتب الاختيارات، ثم علّم الدائرة بجوار الإجابة الصحيحة. من
        <span class="num" dir="ltr"><%= MINOPT %></span> إلى
        <span class="num" dir="ltr"><%= MAXOPT %></span> اختيارات.
      </p>

      <% for (var c = 0; c < optionCount; c++) { %>
      <div class="qchoice<%= qCorrect === String(c) ? " qchoice--correct" : "" %>" data-qchoice>
        <%
        /* The radio carries the answer key by INDEX; the server resolves
           it to the choice's text. It used to be a free-text box that
           had to match one of the choices character-for-character, and
           because grading compares literally, a stray space there scored
           every student zero on the question with nothing on the admin
           side to show why. correctAnswer is still STORED as the text,
           so student-side grading and every existing paper are
           untouched — only the way it is picked has changed. */
        %>
        <input
          class="qchoice__radio"
          type="radio"
          id="q_<%= i %>_c<%= c %>"
          name="q_<%= i %>_correct"
          value="<%= c %>"
          required
          aria-label="الاختيار <%= c + 1 %> هو الإجابة الصحيحة"
          <%= qCorrect === String(c) ? " checked" : "" %>
        />
        <label class="qchoice__label" for="q_<%= i %>_a<%= c %>">
          الاختيار <span class="num" dir="ltr" data-qchoiceno><%= c + 1 %></span>
          <abbr title="مطلوب">*</abbr>
        </label>
        <input
          class="input qchoice__text"
          type="text"
          id="q_<%= i %>_a<%= c %>"
          name="q_<%= i %>_a<%= c %>"
          required
          maxlength="300"
          autocomplete="off"
          value="<%= qAnswers[c] || "" %>"
        />
        <span class="qchoice__flag" aria-hidden="true">صحيحة</span>
        <button class="qchoice__remove" type="button" data-qchoiceremove>
          <span class="sr-only">حذف هذا الاختيار</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <% } %>

      <button class="btn btn--ghost qchoices__add" type="button" data-qchoiceadd>
        + إضافة اختيار
      </button>
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <%
  /* ---- TRUE / FALSE ----------------------------------------------
     Two radios, and nothing else. The option TEXT never appears as an
     input: it is qt.TF_OPTIONS on the server, so the labels here and the
     stored answer key cannot drift apart. This posts an index (0 or 1)
     for the same reason multiple choice does. */
  %>
  <fieldset
    class="qfields"
    data-qfields="truefalse"<%= groupAttrs("truefalse") %><%= groupDisabled("truefalse") %>
  >
    <legend class="sr-only">الإجابة الصحيحة</legend>

    <div class="qchoices qchoices--tf" role="group" aria-label="الإجابة الصحيحة">
      <p class="qchoices__hint">علّم ما إذا كانت العبارة صحيحة أم خاطئة.</p>

      <% TFOPTS.forEach(function (label, n) { %>
      <div class="qchoice<%= qTf === String(n) ? " qchoice--correct" : "" %>" data-qchoice>
        <input
          class="qchoice__radio"
          type="radio"
          id="q_<%= i %>_tf<%= n %>"
          name="q_<%= i %>_tf"
          value="<%= n %>"
          required
          <%= qTf === String(n) ? " checked" : "" %>
        />
        <label class="qchoice__label qchoice__label--tf" for="q_<%= i %>_tf<%= n %>">
          <%= label %>
        </label>
      </div>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <%
  /* ---- EXPLAIN ----------------------------------------------------
     No answer key: nothing here is machine-checkable. The model answer
     is for whoever marks it, and is optional — so no `required`, which
     also means this group is the one that would submit fine even if the
     disabled handling above were wrong. */
  %>
  <fieldset
    class="qfields"
    data-qfields="explain"<%= groupAttrs("explain") %><%= groupDisabled("explain") %>
  >
    <legend class="sr-only">تصحيح السؤال المقالي</legend>

    <%
    /* The mark this question is worth. ONLY Explain questions have one:
       auto-graded questions are worth exactly one mark and ignore the field
       even if a hand-crafted POST sets it, so the input lives inside this
       fieldset — which the browser leaves out of the submission entirely
       while another type is selected.

       NOT `required`, on purpose. A required control inside a hidden group is
       the trap documented at the top of this file, and there is no need to
       take the risk: a blank value falls back to the same default the
       schema uses. */
    %>
    <div class="form-field form-field--sm qcard__max">
      <label class="label" for="q_<%= i %>_max">درجة السؤال</label>
      <input
        class="input input--ltr"
        type="number"
        id="q_<%= i %>_max"
        name="q_<%= i %>_max"
        value="<%= qMax %>"
        min="<%= MINPTS %>"
        max="<%= MAXPTS %>"
        step="1"
        inputmode="numeric"
        autocomplete="off"
      />
      <p class="field-hint">
        من <span class="num" dir="ltr"><%= MINPTS %></span> إلى
        <span class="num" dir="ltr"><%= MAXPTS %></span>. الافتراضي
        <span class="num" dir="ltr"><%= DEFPTS %></span>. يضعها المصحّح للطالب
        من هذه الدرجة.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-field qcard__model">
      <label class="label" for="q_<%= i %>_model">الإجابة النموذجية</label>
      <textarea
        class="input"
        id="q_<%= i %>_model"
        name="q_<%= i %>_model"
        maxlength="2000"
        rows="4"
        autocomplete="off"
      ><%= qq.modelAnswer || "" %></textarea>
      <p class="field-hint">
        اختياري. تظهر لك عند التصحيح فقط، ولا تظهر للطالب أثناء الامتحان.
      </p>
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <div class="form-field qcard__image">
    <label class="label" for="q_<%= i %>_image">صورة السؤال</label>
    <input
      class="input"
      type="file"
      id="q_<%= i %>_image"
      name="q_<%= i %>_image"
      accept="image/*"
    />
    <p class="field-hint">اختياري. PNG أو JPG أو WEBP، بحد أقصى ٥ ميجابايت.</p>
  </div>
</fieldset>
